# 7. MVP Feature Scope

## 7.1 Feature P0 — Upload

Supported:

- JPG/JPEG
- PNG
- WebP

Optional later:

- HEIC
- AVIF

Requirements:

- drag & drop
- click to upload
- paste image from clipboard
- mobile camera/file picker
- file validation
- size validation
- clear error message

Example:

> Drop an image here

> or

> Browse files

Maximum recommended MVP input size:

**20 MB**

This can be adjusted after testing.

---

# 8. Feature P0 — Background Removal

This is the flagship feature.

## User flow

```text
Upload
 ↓
Image preview
 ↓
Remove Background
 ↓
Processing
 ↓
Transparent result
 ↓
Edit background
 ↓
Download
```

## UI

Before processing:

- image preview
- Remove Background button

During processing:

- progress indicator
- estimated stage
- cancel option if technically possible

After processing:

- before/after comparison
- transparent checkerboard background
- background options

Background options:

- Transparent
- White
- Black
- Custom color
- Upload image

---

# 9. Feature P0 — Before/After Comparison

Provide an interactive comparison slider.

Desktop:

```text
+------------------------------+
| BEFORE       | AFTER         |
|              |               |
|      IMAGE   |    IMAGE      |
|              |               |
+------------------------------+
             ◄───●───►
```

Mobile:

The comparison must remain usable with touch.

---

# 10. Feature P0 — Export

Formats:

- PNG
- JPG
- WebP

PNG is the default when transparency exists.

JPG is preferred when the user selects a solid background.

WebP is offered as a smaller modern format.

Export settings:

- quality
- width
- height
- format
- transparent/solid background

Show estimated file size when feasible.

---

# 11. Feature P0 — Resize

Presets:

- Original
- 25%
- 50%
- 75%
- 100%
- Custom width
- Custom height

Controls:

- lock aspect ratio
- width
- height

Validation:

- prevent invalid dimensions
- warn about excessive output dimensions

---

# 12. Feature P0 — Crop

Crop modes:

- Free
- 1:1
- 4:5
- 3:4
- 4:3
- 16:9
- 9:16

Presets should target common social-media and profile-photo requirements.

---

# 13. Feature P1 — AI Upscaling

This should be released after background removal is stable.

Options:

- 2×
- 4×

The system should not simply stretch the image.

It should use an appropriate super-resolution model.

Important UX:

Display a warning for large images:

> AI upscaling can use significant memory and may take longer on mobile devices.

Fallback:

If WebGPU is unavailable, use WASM if the model/performance is acceptable.

If the device is too weak:

> Your device may not be powerful enough for this enhancement. Try a smaller image or use 2× instead of 4×.

---

# 14. Feature P1 — Image Enhancement

Controls:

- Brightness
- Contrast
- Saturation
- Sharpness
- Exposure
- Blur
- Grayscale

These should initially use Canvas/WebGL/WebGPU operations rather than AI.

---

# 15. Feature P1 — Compression

User chooses:

- Low
- Medium
- High
- Custom

Display:

```text
Original: 4.8 MB
Estimated output: 820 KB
```

The goal is not to promise an exact size before encoding.

---

# 16. Feature P1 — Student Presets

This is an important differentiator.

## 16.1 Formal Photo

Preset:

- background removal
- white/red/blue background
- portrait crop
- enhancement
- export

## 16.2 Pas Foto

Presets:

- 2×3
- 3×4
- 4×6

The UI should explain that local institutional requirements can vary.

## 16.3 CV Photo

Preset:

- portrait crop
- clean background
- mild enhancement
- high-quality export

## 16.4 Social Media

Presets:

- Instagram portrait 4:5
- Instagram square 1:1
- Story/Reels 9:16
- YouTube thumbnail 16:9
- LinkedIn profile

---

# 17. Feature P2 — Batch Processing

Example:

```text
Select 20 images
       ↓
Remove Background
       ↓
Processing 8 / 20
       ↓
Download ZIP
```

Use browser-side processing.

Important:

Batch processing should limit concurrency to prevent browser memory crashes.

Example strategy:

- 1–2 images simultaneously on mobile
- 2–4 on desktop

Tune after benchmarking.

---

# 18. Feature P2 — Object Removal

User selects an area using a brush.

Flow:

```text
Upload
 ↓
Brush over object
 ↓
AI/object removal
 ↓
Preview
 ↓
Accept / Retry
```

This is NOT part of MVP.

